title: "HackMatch — US-021: Notification Center — Persistence, Delivery, and Read Sequence"
---
%%{init: {"theme":"base","themeVariables":{"background":"#ffffff","primaryColor":"#e8f1ff","primaryTextColor":"#1f2937","primaryBorderColor":"#3b82f6","lineColor":"#4b5563","secondaryColor":"#f1e8ff","tertiaryColor":"#fff7d6","fontFamily":"Arial, sans-serif"},"sequence":{"useMaxWidth":true,"diagramMarginX":25,"diagramMarginY":18,"actorMargin":34,"width":160,"height":60,"boxMargin":8,"messageMargin":24,"noteMargin":10}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Part as Active verified PART
    participant UI as NotificationBell
    participant API as Notification API and SSE route
    participant Hub as Realtime bridge and participant hub
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Producer as Recruitment or verification producer

    alt SQL recruitment lifecycle producer
        Producer->>DB: Commit domain change and notification row atomically
    else Node verification producer
        Producer->>DB: Validate and persist notification row
    end
    DB-->>Hub: Supabase Realtime INSERT event
    Hub->>Hub: Deduplicate notification ID and route by participant
    opt Recipient has an authorized SSE stream
        Hub-->>API: Publish participant-scoped event
        API-->>UI: SSE notification and fresh unread count
        UI-->>Part: Update bell and feed
    end
    Note over DB,UI: Persistence is authoritative.<br/>Failed or offline push does not remove the stored notification

    Part->>UI: Open notification center
    UI->>API: GET /api/notifications with cursor/filter
    API->>API: Require Firebase, MFA, active verified PART
    API->>DB: Query caller-owned feed and unread count
    DB-->>API: Newest-first page and count
    API-->>UI: Safe no-store response
    UI-->>Part: Loading, feed, empty, or retry state

    alt Mark one read
        Part->>UI: Select or mark notification
        UI->>API: PATCH /api/notifications/:id/read
        API->>DB: Owner-scoped idempotent read RPC
        DB-->>API: Notification, alreadyRead, unreadCount
    else Mark all read
        Part->>UI: Mark all read
        UI->>API: POST /api/notifications/read-all
        API->>DB: Atomic caller-scoped read-all RPC
        DB-->>API: markedCount and unreadCount
    end
    API-->>UI: Server-confirmed read state
    UI-->>Part: Update badge, then deep link re-authorizes target view

    opt SSE unavailable
        UI->>API: Visible-page fallback refresh every 30 seconds
        API->>DB: Reload caller-owned feed and count
        DB-->>UI: Reconciled persisted state
    end

